          "exact": "            Let N ∈ N and let A ⊆ {1, . . . , N } be such that ab + 1 is not squarefree for every pair\n        a, b ∈ A. Sawhney proved that, for all sufficiently large N , the truncated residue class 7 modulo\n        25 is extremal, and the class 18 modulo 25 is also extremal whenever it has the same cardinality\n        [2]. In this note we make the threshold explicit: for every N ≥ 2.64 × 1017 ,\n                                                                         \u0016        \u0017\n                                                                           N + 18\n                              |A| ≤ {n ∈ [N ] : n ≡ 7 (mod 25)} =                   ."
